**How to implement.** Send kit… as semantic messages of the kit window (001 §P `SendKit`; 001 §O 'Kit menu: Send kit…'; the S5.3 mapper's request: Send kit… joins the kit bar, sending a `TableAndElementRotationMsg`; .spec-md §4 'UI': every user step is a semantic message, and the button and the test send the same message; §10.2, §10.4: per-file progress with Cancel, and the completion message updates the model). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6: (1) `KitWindowShell` (step 186) gains, each field documented in one line, `zipPicker : KitZipPicker` (the save dialog, step 198), `archive : KitArchiveProxy` (the zip writer, step 197) and `archiveJobs : KitArchiveJobHost` (runs the send off the UI thread, step 200). `inert` holds `KitZipPicker.none`, `KitArchiveProxy.createInMemory (InMemoryArchiveDisk.create ())` and `KitArchiveJobHost.inert`. A record expression that builds a shell in full becomes a record update of `KitWindowShell.inert`: the shell `ConstructorScene.mount` builds in `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs` (step 189) is `{ KitWindowShell.inert with explorer = ExplorerProxy.system; requestClose = window.Close }`, so the windows keep their behaviour until step 233 composes their real archive, and a test shell built in full becomes such an update. (2) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `kitSend : KitArchiveJobState` after `kitChanges` (step 187), documented in one line (the window's one send, step 200); `initWith` sets it to `KitArchiveJobState.idle`. (3) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `SendKit of FileName` (send the kit to this zip: the Send kit button's message after its save dialog, and how a test sends a kit), `SendKitProgressed of JobProgress`, `SendKitEnded of Result<KitArchiveOutcome, KitArchiveError>` and `CancelSendKit`. (4) Arms. `SendKit zip`: with `kitFolderOpt = None` it sets `kitStatus` to `A kit with no folder cannot be sent.` and starts nothing; while `kitSend.job.isRunning` it answers the model unchanged, one archive job per window; otherwise it calls `model.kitShell.archiveJobs.startArchiveJob (fun observer -> model.kitShell.archive.sendKit model.kit.kitFile folder zip observer)` (step 198), sets `kitSend` to `kitSend.started` of the handle and `kitStatus` to `None`. Sending writes no kit file, so it is not behind the read-only guard (step 185): a kit opened read-only is sent as it is, which is how a reviewer returns a kit (001 §E 'Review round-trip'). `SendKitProgressed p` sets `kitSend` to `kitSend.progressed p`. `SendKitEnded result` sets `kitSend` to `KitArchiveJobState.idle` and `kitStatus` to `The kit was sent: <n> file(s) zipped.` for `Ok (KitArchiveFinished n)`, `Send kit was cancelled: no zip was written.` for `Ok KitArchiveCancelled`, and `The kit could not be sent — <e.describe>` for `Error e`. `CancelSendKit` calls `model.kitSend.cancel ()` and answers the model unchanged; the end message returns it to idle. No queue, retry, overwrite question (the save dialog asks it, step 200) or other message is added. Tests, in `KitWindowModelTests` (step 184), over its folder kits (`openKitAt` under the class's folder) loaded into `initMain ()`, with `kitShell` an update of `KitWindowShell.inert` whose `archive` is `KitArchiveProxy.create ()` (step 199) and whose `archiveJobs` is either `KitArchiveJobHost.immediate` over recorders of the `SendKitProgressed` and `SendKitEnded` messages, which the fact then passes through the update in order, or a test-local deferred host that keeps the job and answers a handle cancelling a source the fact owns. Zips go under the fact's own folder, never inside the kit. `Send kit zips the kit's folder and tells how many files it sent`: `SendKit` of `<fact>/exports/Optics QZ.zip` then the recorded messages leave the zip there; `KitArchiveProxy.create ().listZipEntries` of it holds `.kit-json`, `data` and `library` and no `.oc` entry, though the kit holds `.oc/lock`; `kitStatus` is `The kit was sent: <the zip's file count> file(s) zipped.` and `kitSend` is idle. `a running send shows each zipped file as progress`: after `SendKit` and the first recorded progress only, `kitSend.job.isRunning` holds and its `progressText` starts `1 / `. `a cancelled send writes no zip and says so`: over the deferred host, `SendKit` leaves the job running and no zip; `CancelSendKit` cancels the fact's source; the fact runs the kept job over an observer of that source's token, which answers `Ok KitArchiveCancelled`, and `SendKitEnded` of it sets `kitStatus` to `Send kit was cancelled: no zip was written.`, `kitSend` idle and no zip. `a scratch kit is not sent and no job starts`: over `initMain ()` (the scratch kit), `SendKit` sets `kitStatus` to `A kit with no folder cannot be sent.` and the recorders stay empty. `a send that fails tells why and leaves the window idle`: `SendKit` of a zip inside the kit's folder ends with `kitStatus` containing `inside the kit it holds` and `kitSend` idle. `a kit opened read-only is sent, and its folder is unchanged`: over the kit opened read-only, `SendKit` writes the zip and every file of the kit's folder keeps its bytes.

**Acceptance.** After the Send kit messages land, `SendKit` MUST start one send of the kit's folder through the shell's job host, `SendKitProgressed` and `SendKitEnded` MUST drive `kitSend` and `kitStatus`, and `CancelSendKit` MUST cancel the running send; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `Send kit zips the kit's folder and tells how many files it sent`, `a running send shows each zipped file as progress`, `a cancelled send writes no zip and says so`, `a scratch kit is not sent and no job starts`, `a send that fails tells why and leaves the window idle` and `a kit opened read-only is sent, and its folder is unchanged`, the count rising by 6; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.
